Source: flickos-classroom-view
Section: education
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>
# python3-pil and openssl: the tests make thumbnails and certificates.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3,
               python3-pil,
               openssl
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-classroom-view
Architecture: all
# The program, the student's agent, the strip and a lab computer's service;
# the teacher's window comes with flickos-classroom-teacher, so a student's
# computer has no Classroom in its menu.
# python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the console, the strip and the pairing window
#   (GTK loaded only for a window);
# python3-pil: thumbnails, reduced and saved as JPEG (Debian's grim has no
#   JPEG, phase 0);
# grim: the screen, through zwlr_screencopy;
# openssl: each computer's key and certificate;
# libnotify-bin: the teacher's messages and the first-run notice;
# xdg-utils: a web page the teacher opens;
# flickos-lock (>= 1.4~test1): the class lock (lock --class-message, ADR-007)
#   and the demo in it (--class-image, ADR-014);
# flickos-layouts (>= 1.88~test1): the panel button that shows the screen can
#   be seen (custom/classroom, ADR-004: it can't be hidden);
# flickos-control (>= 1.78~test1): Settings > Classroom (the button opens it),
#   its list of teachers (`student teachers`, ADR-016) and its
#   firewall.classroom, which lets the teacher's computer in;
# systemd: a lab computer's service (ADR-011), enabled only by `lab on`;
# wayvnc, libneatvnc0 (>= 0.9.1+dfsg+flickos1~test1): one screen seen or
#   controlled (ADR-012), started only for that; FlickOS's libneatvnc0 has
#   no H.264, so 1.2 MB instead of Debian's 53 MB (ADR-013);
# gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1: the strip that says a teacher views or
#   controls the screen (ADR-015).
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         python3-pil,
         grim,
         openssl,
         libnotify-bin,
         xdg-utils,
         flickos-lock (>= 1.4~test1),
         flickos-layouts (>= 1.88~test1),
         flickos-control (>= 1.78~test1),
         systemd,
         wayvnc,
         libneatvnc0 (>= 0.9.1+dfsg+flickos1~test1),
         gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: share a FlickOS computer's screen with a teacher
 A student's half of FlickOS Classroom: a paired teacher's computer sees
 this screen, and can lock it with a message, show a message, open a web
 page, or view and control it. Students pair with the teacher's computer by
 typing a six-digit code; a school's lab computers are paired once by an
 administrator.
 .
 Nothing runs until sharing is turned on in Settings > Classroom, and the
 panel always shows when the screen can be seen and when a teacher is
 looking. Nothing is recorded. The teacher's computer needs
 flickos-classroom-teacher. FlickOS computers only.

Package: flickos-classroom-teacher
Architecture: all
# flickos-classroom-view (same version): the program (one program, two roles,
#   ADR-002); this package adds its teacher's window to the menu;
# gir1.2-gtk-vnc-2.0: one student's screen, seen or controlled (Q5).
Depends: flickos-classroom-view (= ${binary:Version}),
         gir1.2-gtk-vnc-2.0,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: see and guide a classroom of FlickOS computers
 The teacher's window of FlickOS Classroom: every paired student's screen
 in a grid; lock the screens with a message, show a message, open a web
 page on every screen, view or control one student's screen, or show the
 teacher's screen in the students' class lock. Students pair with this
 computer by typing a six-digit code.
 .
 Students' computers need only flickos-classroom-view. FlickOS computers
 only.
